   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Binc Stereo — sequence chain (windowed, constant memory)\n\nNo video decode in the graph. Extract the clip to a 16-bit PNG sequence ONCE (keeps 10-bit sources intact):\n\n    ffmpeg -i clip.mp4 -pix_fmt rgb48le ComfyUI/input/frames/f-%05d.png\n\nThen **LOAD WINDOW** reads only `count` frames from `start` → Depth Anything V2 → Temporal Filter → Stereo from Depth → eye L / eye R PNG sequences in `output/binc-stereo/L/` and `/R/`.\n\n- `proxy` = half/quarter runs the whole chain small for a fast QC pass; parallax is in % of width so every setting carries to `full`.\n- Every node prints time, s/frame and a resource line (RSS / MPS or CUDA) in its info/report — no black boxes.\n- Run `start` = 0, 24, 48 … in order (`count` 24). `SaveImage` numbering continues, so each eye folder becomes one continuous sequence.\n- Peak RAM ≈ 24 frames × 4K × a handful of tensors ≈ 6–8 GB. Nothing holds the whole take.\n- Depth is normalised per window; if convergence steps between windows, lower `hi_percentile` or fix lo/hi from the first window's `info`.\n- Check `parallax_vis` first: near objects must read **dark**; if not, flip `depth_polarity`. `report.summary.ok` must be true.\n- Core `SaveImage` writes 8-bit PNG. Assemble: `ffmpeg -framerate 24 -i eyeL_%05d_.png -c:v prores_ks -profile:v 3 -pix_fmt yuv422p10le eyeL.mov`"
   ],
   "title": "READ FIRST"
  },
